COMPILING AND INSTALLING

CAMFR is a C++/Fortran library with a Python 3 interface built on
Boost.Python.

It has been tested on Ubuntu 26.04 with Python 3.14, NumPy 2.3, GCC and
gfortran 15, Boost 1.90, Blitz++ 1.0.2, reference BLAS/LAPACK 3.12 and
SCons 4.8.


Requirements

- Python 3 with its development headers.
- NumPy, Matplotlib and Pillow. SciPy is needed for the RCLED, GARCLED
  and dispersive material helpers.
- A C++ compiler supporting C++17 and a Fortran 77 compiler
  (e.g. g++ and gfortran).
- SCons.
- The Boost Python library, built for the same Python version that will
  run CAMFR (e.g. libboost_python314 for Python 3.14).
- Blitz++ 0.9 or later.
- BLAS and LAPACK. If possible, use an optimised implementation
  (OpenBLAS, Intel MKL, ...) for maximum performance.

On Debian or Ubuntu these can be installed with

  sudo apt install g++ gfortran scons python3-dev python3-venv \
       python3-numpy python3-scipy python3-matplotlib python3-pil \
       python3-pil.imagetk python3-tk libboost-python-dev libblitz0-dev \
       libblas-dev liblapack-dev


Building and installing

Copy a machine configuration template to machine_cfg.py, then install
the package with pip:

  cp machine_cfg.py.linux machine_cfg.py
  python3 -m pip install .

pip runs SCons to build camfr/_camfr.so and installs the 'camfr'
package. machine_cfg.py.linux detects the Python and NumPy include
directories from the interpreter that runs the build, and looks for
Boost in /usr. If Boost.Python is installed elsewhere, point BOOST_ROOT
at its prefix:

  BOOST_ROOT=/opt/boost python3 -m pip install .

By default pip builds in an isolated environment and downloads
setuptools, NumPy and SCons for it. To build against the packages that
are already installed instead, use

  python3 -m pip install --no-build-isolation .

Distributions that mark the system Python as externally managed
(PEP 668) require a virtual environment, e.g.

  python3 -m venv --system-site-packages venv
  venv/bin/pip install --no-build-isolation .

To build the library in place without installing, run 'python3 -m SCons'.

Only machine_cfg.py.linux is provided. The Python 2-era templates for
macOS, MSVC, Gentoo and old gcc were removed; INSTALL.MacOSX and
INSTALL.Windows are kept for reference.


Testing

  cd testsuite
  python3 camfr_test.py

Set MPLBACKEND=Agg to run the tests without a display.
